In response to some recent questions:

The development team's work on NetHack 3.1 is continuing, and it
is on schedule.  In a previous message I said that we do not think
it wise to announce a date of release until we know that we can
deliver by that date.  This is still the case.  We understand the
impatience expressed by some.  But it is not going to be very long
now.

As to NetHack++.  While we still respond to mail about NetHack 3.0,
which comes to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu, NetHack 3.0 is not
maintained by us anymore.  As long as the lisence terms are adhered
to, we take no formal position on such ventures with 3.0.

If there are any misgivings, they involve the undesirability of future
splintering of the game.  There are readers of this newsgroup today
who were not around during the development of 2.3, and they have no
memories of the chaos, the multiple versions, and the confusion that
existed at that time.  This was changed dramatically when we undertook
to develop 3.0.  The systematic collaboration between you and the
development team was spectacular, and so were the results.  It will be
a pity if we fail to do the same with 3.1.

For the development team,

-Izchak



